    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d305">

                <pb facs="0413" n="241" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp01v01/pg241"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72119/504</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Chile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Shea</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-03-15T19:00:00-04:42">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 15, 1917, 7 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 7.30 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>In reply to your telegram March 14, 6 p.m. Minister for Foreign Affairs assures
                    me that Chile will have nothing to do with peace movement being promoted by the
                    Argentine Republic. Brazilian Minister here also assures me that his country
                    will not join the movement. They do not regard it as serious here. No editorial
                    discussion, news despatches generally from Buenos Aires.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Shea</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
